.venv/
__pycache__/
# Written by the MCP framework itself at runtime (the FTS index). Copying a host-built one
# in would ship an index whose cache key does not match this image's HEAD, so it would be
# discarded and rebuilt on the first request anyway.
_meta/.cache/
# 29 MiB of committed text extractions, and the server NEVER opens them. They are the
# provenance evidence corpus-verify-provenance checks `## Full text` against, and that is a
# CI gate run against a checkout, not a container.
#
# Consequence, stated so it is not a surprise: `corpus-verify-provenance` cannot run INSIDE
# this image. Same trade executive-regulatory-frameworks makes.
#
# The source PDFs are not here to exclude — they are gitignored and never committed
# (snapshot_policy: hash-only; one is 182 MiB, over GitHub's per-file limit).
_meta/snapshots/
# Generated at deploy time by the pages workflow; never needed at runtime.
site/
# NOTE: .git is deliberately NOT ignored — it is a RUNTIME dependency. The FTS cache key is
# `git rev-parse HEAD` plus a hash of `git status --porcelain`, and corpus_overview() runs
# `git log -1`. Without it repo_state() collapses to a constant, so content changes are
# never picked up for the life of the process and corpus_overview reports an empty commit —
# silently, in both cases. Build from a depth-1 clone to keep it small.
